<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<div id="p1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:8.5pt;vertical-align:-1.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-8.3pt,0.2pt) scale(0.953918566624486,0.953918566624486) ;">
<p id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention Transfer Is Not Universally Effective for Vision Transformers</span></p>
</span></div>
<p id="p1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:120%;">Technical Appendices and Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
  
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide further implementation details to support reproducibility of our experimental setup below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Details of Model Zoo</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.T1" title="In A.1 Details of Model Zoo ‣ Appendix A Additional Implementation Details ‣ Attention Transfer Is Not Universally Effective for Vision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> summarizes all 20 pre-trained weights from 11 ViT families used in our evaluations, covering three model sizes (Tiny, Small, Base) where official checkpoints are available.
The benchmark spans the major pre-training paradigms in recent ViT representation learning, including
supervised training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>,
self-distillation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>,
contrastive learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>,
multi-modal pre-training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>,
masked image modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>,
and large-scale segmentation pre-training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table A: </span><span id="A1.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-trained Model Zoo.</span>
We present 20 pre-trained weights from 11 well-known ViT families used in our Attention Transfer evaluations.
All weights are with the patch size of 16, while for families only with patch size of 14 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, we interpolate their patch embeddings from 14 to 16.
</figcaption>
